#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100691 :question/id #uuid "da92ef6c-cb0b-5a4c-9a0d-0f0a9db19616" :question/math-academy-id "e-4403" :question/problem "Let\n![](images/53/5357fcb0ec150699b4d50cbd6fa9651c421ac3500660703396146362160328a2.png)\nand\n![](images/63/63d354773d145f05e73e808efe2a21164cb28d6ff19ae104d6bbde6510cf10e6.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = \n\t{\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048297 :topic/math-academy-id 147 :topic/title "Multiplying Square Matrices"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048896 :topic/math-academy-id 861 :topic/title "Introduction to Matrices"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101319 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eee15b20-7670-503f-971f-d56fd86f8528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448504} {:answer/id #uuid "8e36cc5c-ee04-5d14-93c0-5ec4fd6754bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e36cc5c-ee04-5d14-93c0-5ec4fd6754bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448505} :answer-field/id #uuid "73a25775-ae2f-598a-be5f-116f1c5257d3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449292} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a98bec2-fd5b-577d-b1a2-de624a75c4de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448506} {:answer/id #uuid "8f344679-285a-5a78-87d1-893db3de166d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a98bec2-fd5b-577d-b1a2-de624a75c4de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448506} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b90ee4-8516-5880-9f21-2235262ae0b8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449293} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69c941f3-afcf-5dca-a631-aac8dfb757b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448508} {:answer/id #uuid "384c1599-b211-55de-9dff-459dd6139d8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "384c1599-b211-55de-9dff-459dd6139d8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448509} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa235668-87f9-5d4c-8f5d-dd9e00466bf2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449294}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9258b6d8-3a2c-54d4-bc2f-8b9ea4ccd825" :question/math-academy-id "q-22063" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $AB$ is well defined\n- **II.** The product $BA$ is well defined\n- **III.** The product $AC$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{A}_{3\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 1}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ac97073-f2e4-57fa-bc98-21619911b032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477307} {:answer/id #uuid "fed5ba5b-9655-57ac-bf85-e26d4ca80ab6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fed5ba5b-9655-57ac-bf85-e26d4ca80ab6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477308} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9a32b98-4ce8-5ab9-ba0f-52336fc8a891" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab354b54-184d-5e28-ab49-c725761e84d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477309} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7c4fb6-9856-5e08-8e95-baf50093e535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f7c4fb6-9856-5e08-8e95-baf50093e535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477310} :answer-field/id #uuid "579c28da-6262-519a-b610-6fec803beaf2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477624} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f8cc3b1-c6eb-5129-bcad-4e7d08d4a6cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477311} {:answer/id #uuid "88d68881-4ce5-5cc2-8b8b-c3129b170191" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88d68881-4ce5-5cc2-8b8b-c3129b170191" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477312} :answer-field/id #uuid "058434be-b274-586d-9c20-7a526c76c9a3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477625}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59f14d04-9b7d-5b14-8363-a42027c3b11c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42374" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ -0 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statement are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\nI. The product $AB$ is well defined\nII. The product $BA$ is well defined\nIII. The product $AC$ is well defined\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that all three statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265727 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb45ac63-db12-5103-a680-0aca60a50ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448368} {:answer/id #uuid "a12d2978-9d54-59d4-9961-6bdc86f3c49f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb45ac63-db12-5103-a680-0aca60a50ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448368} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0935ce5-8cb9-5439-9df5-d68f6b26b1b4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fb2ec2a-0f20-512b-93a8-4b9f3c962c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448370} {:answer/id #uuid "022054e0-5021-5992-9a69-680cffbd01c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fb2ec2a-0f20-512b-93a8-4b9f3c962c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448370} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2774138-c2fc-5876-84c5-93da8a175e9f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449225} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb2b2b09-edcc-581e-920d-e47a8346fc6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448372} {:answer/id #uuid "c8393209-b177-529e-b28b-4beba3d7980d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8393209-b177-529e-b28b-4beba3d7980d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448373} :answer-field/id #uuid "887210a3-979a-5046-a639-10af689a9ba1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449226}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22b7c2e7-9621-5013-a411-a722a7ceea01" :question/math-academy-id "q-129437" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $RS$ is well defined\n- **II.** The product $RP$ is well defined\n- **III.** The product $SP$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $P$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{5\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $S$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290369 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a93ef54-75a7-58b3-aefb-23905447fd8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450250} {:answer/id #uuid "4b995925-934b-5fd2-877f-aa3cf84a5166" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b995925-934b-5fd2-877f-aa3cf84a5166" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450251} :answer-field/id #uuid "399ae7fe-01e2-5382-b1a9-4e47af718b72" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44ff3d40-849a-5db8-9cf6-5fac0ac794ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450252} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef26044-c1a2-592a-854e-9764c570b332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44ff3d40-849a-5db8-9cf6-5fac0ac794ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450252} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8966769-d214-5dda-9b5c-f23fef8c54ed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451080} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e376649-41c7-5d9c-81ec-516f8c48228b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450254} {:answer/id #uuid "e18e340e-63df-594f-ab82-c85ec74e7f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e18e340e-63df-594f-ab82-c85ec74e7f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450255} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b7bc0c6-04f7-5fcb-9611-2c846635a049" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451081}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f63e1f3-652b-58b6-9207-73ea266277c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-22055" :question/problem "$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $X,Y,$ and $Z?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $XY$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $YX$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $YZ$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $X$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, $Y$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $Z$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $X$ and $2$ rows in $Y.$ Since the number of columns in $X$ equals the number of rows in $Y,$ the matrices $X$ and $Y$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{X}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{Y}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $Y$ and $2$ rows in $X.$ Since the number of columns in $Y$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $X,$ the matrices $Y$ and $X$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{Y}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{X}_{2\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $Y$ and $3$ rows in $Z.$ Since the number of columns in $Y$ equals the number of rows in $Z,$ the matrices $Y$ and $Z$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{Y}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{Z}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbf7dde-3a5a-5e3a-98c4-330f2d78c1ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450256} {:answer/id #uuid "f4fc9501-54e2-5baa-bf12-feec5fed6f1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4fc9501-54e2-5baa-bf12-feec5fed6f1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450257} :answer-field/id #uuid "e46d5a65-585d-5246-84b9-60b6c53ced38" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eac938a0-2f02-528b-aa1f-cd4c2533f774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450258} {:answer/id #uuid "586a9018-9f0f-556a-b600-1b488eba0901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "586a9018-9f0f-556a-b600-1b488eba0901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450259} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fd1e1d7-90e4-552d-8b7f-5890e83db150" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451083} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03abe8a4-3038-556f-860c-4cb48b3a36e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450260} {:answer/id #uuid "036047f5-2b55-5f28-bb20-54fcffca67ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03abe8a4-3038-556f-860c-4cb48b3a36e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450260} :answer-field/id #uuid "826fe441-a593-565f-921b-b7f4ca80e395" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451084}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12577a38-9f6c-5807-b07b-3944030b826c" :question/math-academy-id "q-22056" :question/problem "$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $R,S,$ and $T?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $SR$ is well defined\n- **II.** The product $RS$ is well defined\n- **III.** The product $ST$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $R$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $S$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $T$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $R$ and $2$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $S$ and $3$ rows in $T.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $T,$ the matrices $S$ and $T$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{T}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d3c92a8-562e-563a-8881-3b32d1e12722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450262} {:answer/id #uuid "2aeaf99a-a587-53dc-8e3f-8c29f11b0bdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d3c92a8-562e-563a-8881-3b32d1e12722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450262} :answer-field/id #uuid "5be89768-63a4-500a-973e-77e87c95bbd0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451085} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890358c1-6d1d-54aa-a820-9cbdfd1122e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450264} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e2ca39-1d65-50bc-a2b3-acc534ea6fcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :