 $N.$ Since the number of columns in $L$ equals the number of rows in $N,$ the matrices $L$ and $N$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{L}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{N}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, while statement I is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329647 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b747550b-0a4a-5f3d-86b4-30ddaca87768" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450648} {:answer/id #uuid "f90dfbaa-1eb7-5028-8821-63442d778562" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f90dfbaa-1eb7-5028-8821-63442d778562" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450649} :answer-field/id #uuid "623efc55-bdf4-53da-9936-ec2df1772b9d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7ca6a7b-d2c1-579c-8b4e-c3fc51e76679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450650} {:answer/id #uuid "460bc98c-aa4d-5008-abd2-b4b13e84f625" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7ca6a7b-d2c1-579c-8b4e-c3fc51e76679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450650} :answer-field/id #uuid "5059dfed-f97b-5c68-860f-943b60870dcb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451279} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20fd12d0-0b82-5d63-b678-fdb08097e4e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450652} {:answer/id #uuid "dd3ba80b-43c0-5469-926f-886110b94004" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20fd12d0-0b82-5d63-b678-fdb08097e4e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450652} :answer-field/id #uuid "d414d56d-e135-5893-a7d7-26e4a83fd3f2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451280}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "628bddc5-7db2-5c2d-bca2-c9a2f11c4f87" :question/math-academy-id "q-42381" :question/problem "$$\nO=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OP$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $OR$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $PR$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $P$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $O$ and $2$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $O$ and $1$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $P$ and $1$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statements II and III are false."}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100871 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100693 :question/id #uuid "9352349d-64e0-5437-9d72-7e7f7e571064" :question/math-academy-id "e-4405" :question/problem "Let\n![](images/03/035755bae569c8c9323112891f959076dd727d3ef40ba66c6c40dadf5ddc8f84.png)\nand\n![](images/e5/e53c9ba3bb64b81e44f8f4f49ac77408b7db6ee458be3d43b687d9ed8897ad59.png)\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2 \\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2 \\times 2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{B} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{A} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{BA}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9168374a-e8e8-5258-bb33-1d0eb643cb53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099223} {:answer/id #uuid "b8125a88-3bf5-5e20-b44c-6b3f19b3a07d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\cdot 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099224} {:answer/id #uuid "e3177777-3bfa-53f7-88a0-19af6451e45c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 \\cdot 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099225} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3cf1b4-1e